# Lesson 5, your Exercise 6, completed with East-West cards.
title: Your Exercise 6: partner declines
id: L05-06
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.3
student: S
board: 12
dealer: W
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KJ5    A3     QT74   AJ72
  E  AT86   J54    K9     QT85
  S  Q94    KQT72  J83    94
  W  732    986    A652   K63

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  W Pass
  N 2D     = No 4-card major
  E Pass
  S 2H     = Five hearts, 8-9 points: invitational
  W Pass
  N 2NT    = Minimum, and only two hearts
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = You have told your story
     key: You showed 8-9 points and five hearts. North's 2NT says no to game.
     not 3NT: North has already said no to game. Trust partner.
     not 3H: North has only two hearts, so there is no heart fit.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  2♥ showed five hearts and 8-9 points. North, with a minimum and only two
  hearts, declined with 2NT. If that were enough for game, North would have
  bid it. North is declarer, because North bid no-trump first, and so East
  will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E C5  S C4  W CK  N CA
  2   N HA  E H4  S H2  W H6
      note: Declarer starts on dummy's long hearts, cashing the ace first.
  3   N H3  E H5  S HK  W H8
      note: Continue hearts, crossing to dummy's king.
  4   S HQ  W H9  N D4  E HJ
      note: The jack falls, so all of dummy's hearts are winners.
  5   S HT  W S2  N S5  E S6
      note: Run dummy's good hearts.
  6   S H7  W D2  N D7  E S8
      note: And the last one.
  7   S DJ  W D5  N DT  E DK
      note: Lead toward declarer's Q-10 to knock out a diamond honor.
  8   E CQ  S C9  W C3  N C2
  9   E CT  S S4  W C6  N CJ
  10  N SK  E ST  S S9  W S3
      note: Lead a spade to set up a spade trick.
  11  N C7  E C8  S D3  W D6
      note: Exit with a club: declarer has taken all the tricks available.
  12  E SA  S SQ  W S7  N SJ
  13  E D9  S D8  W DA  N DQ
      note: 8 tricks: 2NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: run dummy's hearts. Cash the ♥A first, the high card from
  the short side, then cross to dummy's hearts.

  2NT made exactly, with five heart tricks from dummy. With nine tricks
  needed, 3NT would have gone down. Trusting partner's 2NT was right.
